    desc: 'The Nouvelle Vague — Truffaut, Godard, Chabrol, Rohmer, Rivette, plus the Left Bank\'s Resnais and Varda — turned film criticism into film style: location Paris streets, natural light, direct address to camera, jump cuts (Breathless\'s famous elisions), long takes of conversation, and genre plots hijacked by cinephile reference. Low budgets and fast crews were the aesthetic: Godard shot Breathless with a wheelchair, a tripod and Chabrol\'s produce-check. The look — black-and-white grain, sunglasses-and-pipe chic, hand-lettered interludes — became the default image of cinematic modernism, and its "camera-stylo" freedom licenses every indie auteur since.',
