    desc: 'The Kirby Krackle — clusters of black dots surrounding energy bursts, cosmic entities and dimensional rifts — is Jack Kirby\'s signature invention, standard from his 1960s-70s Marvel work (Fantastic Four, Fourth World, Eternals). Where other artists used white voids, Kirby packed negative space with crackling dot-masses that read as audible hum and raw force; combined with collage skies, square-fingered gestalt and out-of-panel bursts, the Krackle made machinery of magic. The device is now an industry-wide convention — named, taught in art schools, quoted in Manga (Bleach\'s release energy) and pixel games — and remains the fastest way to draw "power" in ink.',
