    sum: 'Birth certificates as heaven: hearts, birds and fraktur letters inked by country hands.',
    desc: 'Fraktur are the illuminated manuscripts of the Pennsylvania Germans — printed and hand-drawn Taufscheine (birth and baptism certificates), hymn-book bookmarks and house blessings decorated with angels, tulips, unicorns, hearts and birds around Gothic fraktur lettering. Drawing on Rhineland models, scribes and schoolmasters (Scranton, the schoolmaster-artists of Montgomery County) personalized each piece with watercolor brightness that folk-art historians rank with the best American vernacular art. Collections (Free Library of Philadelphia\'s) hold thousands; the motifs — especially the distelfink and tulip — still seed Pennsylvania Dutch craft and quilt design.',
